Best Sunscreen for Oily Skin in India (2026 Guide)
If you have oily skin, you've probably given up on sunscreen at least once — because most formulas leave a greasy film, clog pores, or make your face look shinier by noon. The good news: sunscreen for oily skin doesn't have to feel like that anymore.
The right sunscreen for oily, acne-prone skin in India needs to check three boxes: a lightweight, non-comedogenic formula, a matte or no-white-cast finish, and broad-spectrum SPF 30 or higher to handle Indian sun exposure. Gel-based and water-based sunscreens usually perform better on oily skin than cream-based ones, since they sit on top of the skin without adding extra oil.
Look for ingredients like niacinamide or zinc oxide in the formula — both help control shine while still protecting the skin. Avoid heavy, cream-textured sunscreens, especially ones marketed for 'dry skin' or 'anti-aging,' since these are usually too rich for oily skin types and will worsen breakouts over a humid Indian summer.
Reapplying every 3-4 hours matters more than the price tag — even the best sunscreen stops working after a few hours in the sun, so a lightweight formula you're willing to reapply beats an expensive one you only use once a day.
